{"reviewer_participant_id": "actor:v202d-reviewer-fable-01", "reviews": [{"case_id": "case:19b1842ec3853a54b945", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The governing task declares the complete planned set as the scientific target, and the report's selected result uses the complete planned set (40) as its denominator, matching that target.", "observed_value": "12 / 40 = 30.000 percent", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is the complete planned set of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 24, "end_line": 24, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Confirmed transit detections per planned candidate light curve: 12 / 40 = 30.000 percent."}]}, {"description": "The workflow computes the selected rate with the planned count as the denominator, consistent with the report and the declared target.", "observed_value": "rate = percent(events, planned)", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 42, "end_line": 42, "quoted_text": "rate = percent(events, planned)"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 6, "quoted_text": "The selected rate uses the complete planned set as its\nexposure denominator."}]}, {"description": "Data verification: 40 rows total; 8 rows have baseline_rms_ppm above 1500 (all marked not_analyzed); 12 retained rows are marked yes. The reported counts 40/32/8/12 and the rate 12/40 = 30.000% reproduce exactly.", "observed_value": {"planned": 40, "retained": 32, "removed": 8, "events": 12, "rate_percent": "30.000"}, "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 41, "quoted_text": "star_id,sector,baseline_rms_ppm,transit_detected"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 11, "end_line": 14, "quoted_text": "- Planned candidate light curves: 40\n- Retained after screening: 32\n- Removed by screening: 8\n- Confirmed transit detections among retained curves: 12"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "Potential concern I tested: the numerator (12 events) comes only from the 32 retained curves because the 8 removed curves were never searched, which could be argued to smuggle a subset quantity into a complete-domain claim. However, the report explicitly discloses this, counts the unsearched curves as non-detections in the complete-domain denominator, and bounds the claim as a lower bound, so the denominator and the declared domain agree; this is not the retained-subset-for-complete-domain pattern.", "observed_value": "lower-bound framing with planned denominator", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 28, "end_line": 33, "quoted_text": "The selected rate uses the complete planned set of 40 curves as its exposure\ndenominator, so it applies to the declared target. Because the 8 removed curves\nwere never searched, each is counted in the denominator as a non-detection; the\nrate is therefore a lower bound on the detection rate that full-sensitivity\nvetting of all 40 curves would have produced. No claim is made about the\ndetection rate within the retained subset alone."}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to falsify a no-issue verdict by looking for any place where a retained-subset denominator (32) is presented as applying to the complete planned domain: I recomputed all counts from inputs/data.csv (40 planned, 32 retained, 8 removed, 12 detections), confirmed the selected result uses 40 as the denominator, and checked the scope section for any claim that a 12/32 quantity characterizes the full set. The only subset quantity (12 events among retained) is disclosed and folded into an explicitly bounded lower-bound claim over the full 40. No mismatch between the claimed domain and the exposure denominator survives scrutiny.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:2fc3f9d5e5cc6ccbc719", "verdict": "no_demonstrated_issue_within_scope", "bounded_statement": null, "root_cause": null, "issue_class": null, "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The governing task explicitly declares the retained post-screening subset as the scientific target, so a retained-subset denominator is the correct domain for this case.", "observed_value": "target is the retained post-screening subset", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is explicitly the retained post-screening subset of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow."}]}, {"description": "The selected result uses the retained subset (20) as its denominator and explicitly labels the retained subset as the target, and the closing scope statement disclaims any claim about the complete planned set of 24.", "observed_value": "7/20 = 35.0%", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 12, "end_line": 12, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Among the 20 retained intact roost boxes (the prespecified scientific target; the 4 screened-out boxes from the 24 planned are excluded), 7 showed bat occupancy, an occupancy rate of 35.0% (7/20)."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 14, "end_line": 14, "quoted_text": "All claims here apply only to the retained post-screening subset of 20 intact boxes, not to the complete planned set of 24 boxes."}]}, {"description": "Data verification: 24 rows; 4 rows have condition=damaged (B05, B10, B16, B23); of the 20 intact rows, 7 are occupied=yes (B01, B04, B07, B11, B14, B18, B21). The workflow computes the rate over retained_n, matching the report exactly.", "observed_value": {"planned": 24, "retained": 20, "removed": 4, "occupied": 7, "rate_percent": "35.0"}, "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 19, "end_line": 19, "quoted_text": "rate = Fraction(occupied, retained_n)"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 8, "quoted_text": "- Planned roost boxes: 24\n- Retained after intact-condition screening: 20\n- Removed by screening (damaged or inaccessible): 4\n- Occupancy events among retained boxes: 7"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "Potential concern I tested: 4 of the 24 planned boxes are excluded from the reported rate, which superficially resembles the subset-for-domain pattern. However, the issue class requires a claimed complete-planned-set domain served by a retained-subset denominator; here both the task and the report explicitly and consistently declare the retained subset as the domain, and the planned-unit accounting (24/20/4) is fully disclosed, so no domain/denominator mismatch exists.", "observed_value": "declared domain = retained subset = denominator", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "whose scientific target is explicitly the retained post-screening subset of observation units"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 14, "end_line": 14, "quoted_text": "All claims here apply only to the retained post-screening subset of 20 intact boxes, not to the complete planned set of 24 boxes."}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to falsify the no-issue verdict by searching the report for any sentence that generalizes the 35.0% rate to the complete planned set of 24 boxes, and by recomputing all counts from inputs/data.csv (24 planned, 4 damaged, 20 intact, 7 occupied). Every claim in the report is scoped to the 20 retained boxes, the denominator is 20, and the task itself defines the retained subset as the scientific target. No statement extends the subset rate to the complete planned domain, so the issue class cannot be demonstrated here.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}, {"case_id": "case:a4868f1e140f06a46af9", "verdict": "demonstrated_issue", "bounded_statement": "The report's selected result claims to be the confirmed transit detection rate for the complete planned set of 40 candidate light curves (the domain declared by both the task and the report's own Scientific target section), but the rate is computed as 12/32 = 37.500 percent using only the 32 curves retained after photometric screening as the denominator. Computed over the declared complete-domain denominator of 40, the same event count yields 30.000 percent, so the retained-subset rate overstates the complete-domain rate by 7.5 percentage points while being labeled as the complete-domain rate, with no protocol amendment or approved deviation (the report itself states none exists).", "root_cause": "workflow/analysis.py computes the selected rate with the retained-subset count as the denominator (rate = percent(events, n_retained), 12/32) while the report text labels that rate as the detection rate 'for the complete planned set of 40 candidate light curves', producing a domain/denominator mismatch in the headline claim.", "issue_class": "issue-class:retained-subset-for-complete-domain", "evidence_atoms": [{"description": "The task and the report's Scientific target section both declare the complete planned set of 40 curves as the scientific target of the reported rate.", "observed_value": "complete planned set of 40", "source_spans": [{"path": "task.md", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 1, "quoted_text": "Report one occurrence rate whose scientific target is the complete planned set of observation units, using the planned-unit accounting supplied with this workflow."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 7, "quoted_text": "The scientific target is the complete planned set of 40 candidate light curves\nselected for transit vetting, including the curves that the prespecified\nscreening step removed."}]}, {"description": "The selected result labels the rate as belonging to the complete planned set of 40 while the arithmetic uses the retained-subset denominator of 32, and the scope section confirms this mismatch explicitly.", "observed_value": "12 / 32 = 37.500 percent, labeled as the rate for all 40", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 24, "end_line": 24, "quoted_text": "[selected-result] Confirmed transit detection rate for the complete planned set of 40 candidate light curves: 12 / 32 = 37.500 percent."}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 28, "end_line": 31, "quoted_text": "The selected rate is reported as the detection rate of the complete planned set\nof 40 candidate light curves. Its exposure denominator is the 32 curves retained\nafter screening. No protocol amendment and no approved method deviation exists\nfor this analysis."}]}, {"description": "The workflow source computes the selected rate over the retained subset, not the planned set, and its docstring states this design.", "observed_value": "rate = percent(events, n_retained)", "source_spans": [{"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 42, "end_line": 42, "quoted_text": "rate = percent(events, n_retained)"}, {"path": "workflow/analysis.py", "start_line": 5, "end_line": 6, "quoted_text": "The selected rate uses the retained post-screening subset\nas its exposure denominator."}]}, {"description": "Data verification: inputs/data.csv contains 40 rows; 8 have baseline_rms_ppm above 1500 (TIC-0004, -0009, -0013, -0018, -0024, -0029, -0033, -0038, all marked not_analyzed); 12 retained rows are marked yes. So 12/32 = 37.500 percent (as reported) versus 12/40 = 30.000 percent over the declared complete domain.", "observed_value": {"planned": 40, "retained": 32, "events": 12, "reported_rate": "37.500", "complete_domain_rate": "30.000"}, "source_spans": [{"path": "inputs/data.csv", "start_line": 1, "end_line": 41, "quoted_text": "star_id,sector,baseline_rms_ppm,transit_detected"}, {"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 11, "end_line": 14, "quoted_text": "- Planned candidate light curves: 40\n- Retained after screening: 32\n- Removed by screening: 8\n- Confirmed transit detections among retained curves: 12"}]}], "counterevidence_atoms": [{"description": "Strongest counterargument I tested: the report transparently discloses that the exposure denominator is the 32 retained curves, so a careful reader could recover the mismatch. However, disclosure does not repair the claim itself: the tagged selected result still asserts that 37.500 percent is the detection rate 'for the complete planned set of 40', and the report affirms no amendment redefined the target, so the headline claim remains a retained-subset rate presented for the complete domain.", "observed_value": "denominator disclosed but claim domain unchanged", "source_spans": [{"path": "results/report.md", "start_line": 28, "end_line": 31, "quoted_text": "The selected rate is reported as the detection rate of the complete planned set\nof 40 candidate light curves. Its exposure denominator is the 32 curves retained\nafter screening. No protocol amendment and no approved method deviation exists\nfor this analysis."}]}], "falsification_attempt": "I tried to falsify the demonstrated-issue verdict three ways. First, I checked whether any language in the report rescopes the selected result to the retained subset (e.g., a lower-bound or subset-only framing as in a correctly bounded report); there is none — the selected result and the scope section both assert the rate is 'of the complete planned set of 40'. Second, I checked whether an amendment or approved deviation could legitimize a retained-subset denominator for the complete-domain claim; the report explicitly states none exists. Third, I recomputed from the raw data to rule out a labeling typo: 32 retained and 12 detections are correct, so 12/32 = 37.500 percent is genuinely the retained-subset rate, and the complete-domain rate under the declared target would be 12/40 = 30.000 percent. All three attempts failed to overturn the verdict.", "cross_case_evidence_used": false, "unresolved_material_questions": [], "self_reported_confidence": "high"}]}